From 52878c2ab3f68142d599731806a36f1df36837a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:10:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 57/57] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: Feed dispcc from the
 active-only XO
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DSI PHY keeps its "iface" clock (disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk) under pm_clk,
which prepares it at probe and keeps it prepared. Its source,
disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk_src, runs from the dispcc XO input, and with that
input on RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC the APSS keeps a sleep-set vote on the XO
through system suspend, so the SoC never reaches XO shutdown or vmin.

The display clock controller only needs the XO while the CPUs are
running. Use RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC, which votes in the active set only.

Tested on the F(x)tec Pro1-X (QX1050) with the PSCI system idle state:
with RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC, bi_tcxo stays prepared through suspend and RPM
vmin count stays 0 (74.9 mA); with RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC, nothing
holds bi_tcxo, the SoC is in vmin for about 85% of a 5 minute sleep
window and the battery draw drops to 37-40 mA.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model found it from clock prepare counts captured in noirq suspend; tested on the device by the model)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=model; retrieval=none
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
index 615f1181c..445d7fae4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
@@ -2367,7 +2367,7 @@ mdss_dsi0_phy: phy@5e94400 {
 		dispcc: clock-controller@5f00000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sm6115-dispcc";
 			reg = <0x0 0x05f00000 0 0x20000>;
-			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC>,
+			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC>,
 				 <&sleep_clk>,
 				 <&mdss_dsi0_phy DSI_BYTE_PLL_CLK>,
 				 <&mdss_dsi0_phy DSI_PIXEL_PLL_CLK>,
